\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces PRISMA 2020 flow of the study selection. The 2{,}340 and the 3{,}807 are identifier lists. They share 364 papers, and their union is the 5{,}783. The included phase continues through the auxiliary screen, the removal of overlapping identifiers, the removal of two pre-1994 studies, and the human re-screen. The mapped set is 455 studies (Table~\ref {tab:ledger}). The 318-study joint tables are an older cut (381 records minus 63 duplicates) and are not a node of this flow. In the original run, 595 records with no abstract and 16 records that stayed pending were closed under EC5; this revision re-screened those records.}}{19}{figure.caption.38}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:prisma}{{1}{19}{PRISMA 2020 flow of the study selection. The 2{,}340 and the 3{,}807 are identifier lists. They share 364 papers, and their union is the 5{,}783. The included phase continues through the auxiliary screen, the removal of overlapping identifiers, the removal of two pre-1994 studies, and the human re-screen. The mapped set is 455 studies (Table~\ref {tab:ledger}). The 318-study joint tables are an older cut (381 records minus 63 duplicates) and are not a node of this flow. In the original run, 595 records with no abstract and 16 records that stayed pending were closed under EC5; this revision re-screened those records}{figure.caption.38}{}}
