\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Round-1 human-vs-LLM confusion on a stratified random 20\% sample (human rater as gold standard; counts, not percentages). Recall and Lost Evidence (1$-$Recall) use Wilson 95\% confidence intervals. The T/A row labelled ``maybe$\rightarrow $positive'' treats LLM \texttt  {maybe} decisions as positive referrals, matching LLM4SCREENLIT~R6. The row ``FT (withdrawn)'' is not a screening result: Recall 0.246 records whether a PDF was on disk. The Recall of this revision is 0.630 on the working-set sample (Table~\ref {tab:r2-confusion}). That 0.630 is not a full-text Recall.}}{34}{table.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:human-confusion}{{18}{34}{Round-1 human-vs-LLM confusion on a stratified random 20\% sample (human rater as gold standard; counts, not percentages). Recall and Lost Evidence (1$-$Recall) use Wilson 95\% confidence intervals. The T/A row labelled ``maybe$\rightarrow $positive'' treats LLM \texttt {maybe} decisions as positive referrals, matching LLM4SCREENLIT~R6. The row ``FT (withdrawn)'' is not a screening result: Recall 0.246 records whether a PDF was on disk. The Recall of this revision is 0.630 on the working-set sample (Table~\ref {tab:r2-confusion}). That 0.630 is not a full-text Recall}{table.caption.49}{}}
